        body: "Every lithium-ion cell plant lives or dies on its dry rooms — spaces held at −40°C dew point or lower, continuously, because moisture turns electrolyte salt into hydrofluoric acid and ruins cells. The engineering is desiccant-wheel dehumidification with regeneration heat, vapor-tight envelopes with sealed penetrations, interlocked airlocks, and positive pressure — sized from a moisture balance, not a cooling load. Dry-room qualification at summer design conditions, witnessed and documented, is the signature commissioning event. It's the most specialized HVAC in industrial construction, and the most expensive to fix if it's designed wrong.",
