        heading: "Hazardous-materials classification and control areas",
        body: "The IBC/IFC hazardous-materials framework decides how much of what can sit where: control-area calculations per room, occupancy classification, classified electrical areas, and separation distances. Battery plants concentrate NMP solvent, flammable electrolyte, and reactive lithium — each with its own quantity limits, storage rules, and protection requirements. The hazmat inventory is built with the owner's process team and kept current through design, because the most common permit-review failure is an inventory that doesn't match the process description. Get the classification right early and the AHJ review confirms; get it wrong and the review restarts.",
