        heading: "The battery-plant picture in Illinois",
        body: "Illinois' battery bet centers on Manteno, where Gotion is building a $2 billion, 1.5-million-square-foot LFP operation — pack lines running with a 40 GWh nameplate ambition and a focus on battery energy storage systems as the market pivots. The Chicago-area industrial base, workforce, and logistics network give cell and pack projects a deep bench of process trades. Illinois has real cell-production projects on the ledger — which means the engineering questions here are concrete: dry-room capacity for the announced GWh, utility interconnection for hundred-megawatt loads, and phased designs that get line one producing while later phases build.",
