        body: "Cathode production runs on NMP solvent — effective, recoverable, and hazardous: combustible with reproductive toxicity. Coating and drying areas need solvent-rated ventilation, LEL monitoring with interlocks, classified electrical installations, and recovery systems that condense NMP from drying-oven exhaust for reuse. Recovery is both environmental compliance and operating economics — reclaimed solvent displaces purchased solvent. The hazmat inventory, control-area calculations, and classified-area plans are set during schematic design, because they dictate room layouts that are brutal to retrofit.",
