        heading: "Structural design for process loads",
        body: "Gigafactory structure serves the process, not just the code: heavy concentrated loads from coating lines and ovens, vibration limits for coating uniformity and assembly precision, crane and material-handling dynamics across long bays, and column grids that stay clear of process lines. Most plants are phased, so foundations and framing are detailed for future bays from day one — expansion joints placed where phase two attaches, crane runways pre-planned for extension. The structure also carries the vapor-tight dry-room envelope and the fire-protection strategy's rated separations. Process equipment data shapes the framing; the framing never just follows the shell.",
