        body: "Oregon's play is advanced manufacturing powered by Columbia River hydropower — the Hillsboro silicon-forest ecosystem brings semiconductor-grade cleanroom and process-utility expertise that transfers directly to dry rooms and electrode manufacturing. Portland's industrial districts offer supplier and pack-assembly positioning for the Pacific Northwest battery corridor. Oregon hasn't announced a cell gigafactory — and that's stated plainly, because inventing projects is how developers get burned. The engineering opportunity here is real anyway: oregon's play is advanced manufacturing powered by columbia river hydropower — the hillsboro silicon-forest ecosystem brings semiconductor-grade cleanroom and process-utility expertise that transfers directly to dry rooms and electrode manufacturing. We engineer for the market that exists, not the press release.",
