        body: "A lithium-ion cell in thermal runaway releases flammable gas, extreme heat, and projectiles — and propagates cell to cell. Battery plants answer with zoned fire protection: very-early-warning detection and gas detection in formation and storage, suppression matched to each hazard (solvent areas, high-piled finished-battery warehouses, process halls), explosion control where deflagration is credible, and NFPA 855 governing the storage portions. The strategy is developed during schematic design because suppression water supply, drainage, containment, and rated separations shape the architecture and structure — deciding late means cutting into a framed building.",
