        body: "Wyoming offers America's cheapest industrial power — coal, gas, wind, and utility-scale solar on some of the emptiest, most buildable land in the country. The state's trona and rare-earth exploration adds a materials angle, but the real pitch is energy cost and speed: big parcels, fast permits, no nonsense. Wyoming hasn't announced a cell gigafactory — and that's stated plainly, because inventing projects is how developers get burned. The engineering opportunity here is real anyway: wyoming offers america's cheapest industrial power — coal, gas, wind, and utility-scale solar on some of the emptiest, most buildable land in the country. We engineer for the market that exists, not the press release.",
