        heading: "Utility interconnection: the schedule driver",
        body: "For multi-hundred-megawatt loads, the utility interconnection process — application, system-impact study, facilities study, agreement, construction — routinely spans years, and substation or transmission construction adds more. Site selection that ignores this ends with a permitted building and no power. The engineering deliverable is a utility data package the utility can actually plan from: total demand, 24-hour load shape, power factor and harmonics, and the phased ramp schedule. We open utility coordination in week one and stay in the room through the studies, because the assumptions baked into a system-impact study become the constraints the plant lives with.",
