        body: "Pennsylvania's industrial base is going electric: the Pittsburgh region's steel-to-battery-metals story includes processing plays, while the Philadelphia corridor's pharma cleanroom trades transfer to dry rooms. Abundant natural gas keeps industrial power costs competitive, and the I-76/I-78 corridors offer big-parcel sites within a day of every Northeast market. Pennsylvania hasn't announced a cell gigafactory — and that's stated plainly, because inventing projects is how developers get burned. The engineering opportunity here is real anyway: pennsylvania's industrial base is going electric: the pittsburgh region's steel-to-battery-metals story includes processing plays, while the philadelphia corridor's pharma cleanroom trades transfer to dry rooms. We engineer for the market that exists, not the press release.",
