        heading: "Commissioning and dry-room qualification",
        body: "Commissioning proves the building can hold the process environment before production material is at risk: systems startup, functional testing against design criteria, integrated testing under real combined loads, then process qualification proving yield. The signature event is dry-room qualification — demonstrating continuous −40°C dew point at summer design humidity, full occupancy, maximum door cycles, witnessed and documented. Dry rooms that were value-engineered during construction fail here, publicly, with production material waiting. The qualification tests are written during design, so there's no negotiation about what passing means when the schedule is screaming.",
