        body: "Gigafactories are always fast-tracked: foundations release while process areas are still being designed, equipment procurement overlaps permit review. Done right, phased bid packages — site/civil and foundations first, process areas as equipment selections land — keep construction moving without building on assumptions. Done wrong, overlapping phases without frozen criteria manufactures rework: foundations poured for equipment that changed, utilities routed around process areas that moved. The phasing plan is itself an engineering deliverable — what releases when, what each package assumes, and what happens if an assumption changes.",
